{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/projects/lab-skills/","source":"students/subjects/physics/projects/lab-skills.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Laboratory Technique | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/projects/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Projects</a></nav>\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Laboratory Technique</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Data collection, uncertainty estimation and basic graphing practices for physics labs.</p>\n\n      <h3 class=\"mt-6 text-md font-semibold\">Practice</h3>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Given repeated length measurements: 1.02, 1.00, 1.03, estimate the mean and standard uncertainty (use sample stdev/√n).</p>\n\n      <h3 class=\"mt-4 text-md font-semibold\">Brief solution</h3>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Mean ≈ 1.0167 m; sample stdev ≈ 0.0153 m → uncertainty ≈ 0.0153/√3 ≈ 0.0088 m.</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-green-50 to-lime-50 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif} .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(16px);backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}